  {
    "_comment": "Input/acceptance parity cases for one Appearance record. Consumed by backend/tests/test_composition_documents.py and frontend/src/composition/appearance.test.ts so the Python and TypeScript parsers cannot drift. Cases where accept is false must be refused by all three gates: the Pydantic model, the browser parser, and the generated JSON Schema. JSON has one number type, so `45.0` and `45` are the same document to a browser; integral floats are accepted and fractional ones are not. Several cases exist because lax Pydantic would coerce a value the browser rejects (`\"45\"` for an int, `\"yes\"`/`1` for a bool), which is why those fields are declared `strict=True`. Lengths are counted in CODE POINTS on every gate: the browser must not use `.length`, which counts UTF-16 units and diverges on astral characters.",
